{"question_id": "0a34ad58", "type": "single-session-preference", "label": false, "judge": "No.", "question": "I\u2019m a bit anxious about getting around Tokyo. Do you have any helpful tips?", "gold": "The user would prefer responses that utilize their existing resources, such as their Suica card and TripIt app, to provide personalized tips for navigating Tokyo's public transportation. They might not prefer general tips or recommendations that do not take into account their prior preparations.", "hypothesis": "Getting around Tokyo can be a bit overwhelming at first, but it's quite manageable with some preparation. Here are some helpful tips:\n\n1. **Use Public Transportation**: Tokyo has an extensive and efficient public transportation system, including trains and subways. The JR Yamanote Line is particularly useful as it circles central Tokyo and connects major districts.\n\n2. **Get a Suica or Pasmo Card**: These prepaid IC cards make traveling on trains, subways, and buses easy. You can load money onto the card and simply tap it at ticket gates.\n\n3. **Plan Your Routes**: Use apps like Google Maps or Hyperdia to plan your routes. They provide real-time information on train schedules, platform numbers, and transfer options.\n\n4. **Learn Basic Station Names**: Familiarize yourself with the names of key stations and neighborhoods you plan to visit. This will help you navigate more confidently.\n\n5. **Follow Signage**: Most train stations have English signage, making it easier for non-Japanese speak", "judge_model": "openai/gpt-4o-2024-08-06", "provider": "OpenAI"}
{"question_id": "38146c39", "type": "single-session-preference", "label": false, "judge": "No.", "question": "I've been feeling like my chocolate chip cookies need something extra. Any advice?", "gold": "The user would prefer responses that build upon their previous experimentation with turbinado sugar, suggesting ingredients or techniques that complement its richer flavor. They might not prefer generic cookie-making advice or suggestions that don't take into account their existing use of turbinado sugar.", "hypothesis": "To elevate your chocolate chip cookies, consider these tips:\n\n1. **Add a pinch of sea salt**: Sprinkling a little flaky sea salt on top before baking enhances the chocolate flavor and adds a nice contrast.\n2. **Use brown butter**: Browning the butter before adding it to the dough gives a nutty, rich flavor that can take your cookies to the next level.\n3. **Incorporate different types of chocolate**: Mix in dark chocolate chips, milk chocolate, or even white chocolate for a more complex flavor.\n4. **Add nuts**: Chopped walnuts or pecans can add crunch and depth to your cookies.\n5. **Experiment with extracts**: A splash of vanilla extract or even almond extract can enhance the overall flavor.\n6. **Chill the dough**: Letting the dough chill in the fridge for at least an hour (or overnight) can improve the texture and flavor of the cookies.\n7. **Mix in spices**: A dash of cinnamon or espresso powder can add warmth and depth to the flavor profile.\n\nTry one or a combination of these suggesti", "judge_model": "openai/gpt-4o-2024-08-06", "provider": "OpenAI"}
